    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23YPHZgtrQdmM3x3d757z7z)_\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Problem (found after #459):** `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex` opened a `special-mode` buffer, not an Org-like batch report, so `C-c ?` and the echo-area hints did nothing useful and `d`/`u`/`b`/`k` were missing.\n- #459 is already merged, so this is a new PR on `main`.\n- **Change:** `sp-author-notes-bibtex-report-mode` now derives from `sp-batch-report-mode` (same as the footnote lint, tag lint and notes filing reports).\n  - The buffer is opened with `sp-batch-report-open`: Org text, one heading per author note, one line per entry.\n  - `d` / `u` drop and restore entries, `g` refreshes (keeps the dropped ones), `b` / `D` / `k` / `q` as in every report.\n  - Own keys stay: `RET` visit entry, `o` visit author note, `c` create litnote, `C` create for all exact. On a heading they act on its first entry.\n  - New buffer-local `sp-batch-report-extra-hints`: a derived mode adds its hints with it; they appear before `b Backups`.\n- Docs updated as bullet lists (`sp-org-lint.org`, `sp-batch-report.org`); `.el` files match the docs. `when-let*` only; no CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Tested (Emacs 29.3, batch):** `sp-batch-report-test` 21 pass; `sp-author-notes-bibtex-test` 16 pass (report test now checks the mode, Org, hints, no header line, and a drop). Byte-compile shows only the old docstring-width warnings.\n- **Untested by Claude:** the real GUI and your vault/BibTeX files.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 485-author-works-batch-report; git checkout 485-author-works-batch-report`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [x] `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex`: the buffer is Org-like (headings fold with `TAB`), mode line shows the report mode, no key line in the buffer\n- [x] The echo area shows the hints (`RET`, `d`, `u`, `g`, `o`, `c`, `C`, `b`, `D`, `k`, `q`); `C-c ?` shows them again after another message\n- [x] `RET` on an entry visits the `.bib` entry; `o` visits the author note\n- [x] `d` on an entry: it moves to \"Dropped from the list\"; `u` brings it back; `g` keeps it dropped\n- [x] `c` on an entry asks, creates the litnote, and the report refreshes (the dropped entries stay dropped)\n- [ ] `C` on a heading or an entry creates the litnotes for the exact ones of that author\n- [ ] `RET`, `o`, `c` on a heading act on its first entry\n- [x] No unmatched works: the buffer says \"none\"\n- [x] Regression: `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex-author` (one author report), `sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun`, footnote lint hints are unchanged\n- [ ] Switch to another buffer: no stray hints there\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`\n- Optionally `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 485-author-works-batch-report`\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- The report only reads; `c` / `C` create litnotes, so delete any made while testing\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAF6gJZsaMTJLEA9cM)_",
